Title: Skill case notes: cases chosen by judged usefulness, not four fixed slots (design note)
Created: 2026-11-01
Author: reviewer

--- log ---
2026-11-01T20:18Z reviewer created
2026-11-01T20:19Z reviewer author 2026-11-01: "Variable number of cases then. Observed, not invented!" No fixed count; every case is an observed, sourced episode (journal, ticket, PR, commit), never a composed or blended story; an aggregate stays only if it is itself a recorded measurement.

--- body ---
## Context
Author, 2026-11-01, while refreshing memory/skills/merge.md: "I want agentic judgment on which
memories likely useful." conception/2026-10-31-skill-case-notes.md prescribes four fixed slots
(most recent, usual, best, worst). The merge.md refresh (ticket 1394's closing PR) already chose
its cases by judged usefulness, with one "Use:" line per case naming the decision it changes.

## Scope
Amend the design note: a case note holds the dated, sourced cases most likely to change what an
agent running the skill does next (a trap, a normal friction, an author stance). The four slots
become a guide, not a quota. Each case carries a "Use:" line. The word cap and the
dated-and-sourced requirement stay.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] conception/2026-10-31-skill-case-notes.md states the selection principle and the "Use:" line
- [ ] Any test or script that assumes exactly four slots (scripts/skill-case-notes.sh, tests) agrees
